The '''Regent of the Kingdom of Galwa''' was a position established during the minority of [[Cali IV]], the first king of the post-split [[Burawi Kingdom of Galwa]]. The regent exercised full royal authority on behalf of the minor king, governing the kingdom through the [[Council of Regents (Galwa)|Council of Regents]].

The regency lasted from the [[Burawa Imperial Split|Imperial Split]] of 1709 until the death of Regent Sahra in 1740, at which point Cali IV assumed direct rule.

